{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1089","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"I. Interval-Free Permutations"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1.5 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"512 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Consider a permutation $$$p_1, p_2, \\dots p_n$$$ of integers from 1 to $$$n$$$. We call a sub-segment $$$p_l, p_{l+1}, \\dots, p_{r-1}, p_{r}$$$ of the permutation an "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"interval"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if it is a reordering of some set of consecutive integers. For example, the permutation $$$(6,7,1,8,5,3,2,4)$$$ has the intervals $$$(6,7)$$$, $$$(5,3,2,4)$$$, $$$(3,2)$$$, and others. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each permutation has some trivial intervals — the full permutation itself and every single element. We call a permutation "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"interval-free"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if it does not have non-trivial intervals. In other words, interval-free permutation does not have intervals of length between 2 and $$$n - 1$$$ inclusive. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Your task is to count the number of interval-free permutations of length $$$n$$$ modulo prime number $$$p$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first line of the input there are two integers $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 400$$$) and $$$p$$$ ($$$10^8 \\le p \\le 10^9$$$) — the number of test cases to solve and the prime modulo. In each of the next $$$t$$$ lines there is one integer $$$n$$$ ($$$1 \\le n \\le 400$$$) — the length of the permutation. "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each of $$$t$$$ test cases print a single integer — the number of interval-free permutations modulo $$$p$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4 998244353\n1\n4\n5\n9\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1\n2\n6\n28146\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1 437122297\n20\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n67777575\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For $$$n = 1$$$ the only permutation is interval-free. For $$$n = 4$$$ two interval-free permutations are $$$(2,4,1,3)$$$ and $$$(3,1,4,2)$$$. For $$$n = 5$$$ — $$$(2,4,1,5,3)$$$, $$$(2,5,3,1,4)$$$, $$$(3,1,5,2,4)$$$, $$$(3,5,1,4,2)$$$, $$$(4,1,3,5,2)$$$, and $$$(4,2,5,1,3)$$$. We will not list all 28146 for $$$n = 9$$$, but for example $$$(4,7,9,5,1,8,2,6,3)$$$, $$$(2,4,6,1,9,7,3,8,5)$$$, $$$(3,6,9,4,1,5,8,2,7)$$$, and $$$(8,4,9,1,3,6,2,7,5)$$$ are interval-free."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The exact value for $$$n = 20$$$ is 264111424634864638. "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"I","problemCode":"1089I","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1089/problem/I"}